## Given two strings s and t, return true if the two strings are anagrams of each other, otherwise return false. 
## An anagram is a string that contains the exact same characters as another string, but the order of the characters can be different.
## Since the order of the characters can be different, the easiest way (that I thought of) is to sort the strings into alphabetical order
## Then, I can check if the lists are the same. 
  ## If they are, it returns true and if not, it returns false
  

class Solution:
    def isAnagram(self, s: str, t: str) -> bool:

        list_s = sorted(s)
        list_t = sorted(t)

        if list_s == list_t:
            return True
        else:
            return False
